-
-## D1 — validate provenance at the selected generator boundary
-
-**Choice.** `generate` now requires `type(seed) is int`,
-`type(sample_index) is int and sample_index >= 0`, and difficulty in
-`{None, "easy", "medium", "hard"}`. Bool is rejected despite being an `int`
-subclass. Negative integer seeds remain valid.
-
-**Rationale.** The baseline strict-scalar detector reproduced 39 warnings across
-three difficulty contexts. Bad metadata reached keyed sampling and could create
-records whose apparent provenance could not be replayed consistently across
-languages or serializers.
-
-**Alternatives rejected.** I did not coerce strings/floats, because silent
-normalization hides malformed training records. I did not edit shared `gen_ctx`
-in this task-limited return; that would affect every generator and needs a shared
-migration decision. I did not bump `VERSION`, because lawful inputs retain the
-same output mapping.
-
-**Failure modes and limits.** This local fix does not repair other generators
-that rely on permissive shared context handling. F1 proposes the shared gate.
-
-## D2 — preserve the period declaration and supply executable coverage
-
-**Choice.** Keep `LESSON_SCHEDULE_PERIOD = 4`; enumerate all starts at seed 0 in
-all three bands and pass the source-bound receipt into the final battery.
-
-**Rationale.** Removing the declaration would silence the warning while losing a
-useful curriculum contract. A smoke sample is not evidence that every schedule
-start and held-out query position is identifiable.
-
-**Alternatives rejected.** I did not claim the existing task-local unit test was
-a semantic-gate receipt. I did not treat the 300-lesson random census as an
-exhaustive period check; the separate 12-lesson/60-rotation enumeration provides
-that fixed-seed evidence.
-
-**Failure modes and limits.** The receipt proves the declared starts only at one
-seed and against declared rivals. The 300-lesson census broadens sampling but is
-still finite.
-
-## D3 — use spiral direction as the small rule parameter
-
-**Choice.** Add a separate episode-level `spiral_direction` parameter with
-`clockwise` (canonical default) and `counterclockwise` values. Keep the same
-start cell, container analysis, empty-row count, colors, 3×3 shape, and prefix
-encoding.
-
-**Rationale.** Direction is a nearby meaningful behavior: demonstrations must
-identify an ordering, not just a cosmetic palette. The canonical setting embeds
-the exact selected Racket source and normalizes to the selected rule hash.
