 Record design decisions, hypotheses, review findings, and unresolved questions here.
 Imported associated notes retain original evidence/timestamps in `evidence/associated_notes.jsonl`.
+
+## Current bounded teaching audit: parity coverage remains unresolved
+
+Outcome: **prototype**. The task-local probe and proposed demonstration guard
+do not change production. Generator SHA-256 remains
+`4b9c54dab9598576bce6f4b62439dd23581b7e7ca865ca7f1ee403f75d12a186`;
+canonical normalized rule hash remains `30f91a42c7e5`. No approval or admission
+was requested or granted.
+
+A concrete **ordinary generated lesson** exposes a parity-teaching gap. With
+seed 1, default difficulty, no overrides, and demonstration indices 0–2, all
+three demonstration heights are odd: 9, 7, and 9. A rival copies source row
+`r` to `2*(h//2)-r`, always reserving one center row, and clips destinations
+outside the original canvas. It preserves the input and matches all three
+complete demonstration outputs. It disagrees on query index 3 (height 6),
+first at `(3,0)` where the reference gives 9 and the rival 0; it also disagrees
+on query index 6 (height 8), first at `(4,0)` with the same 9/0 difference.
+This is a generated witness, not an authored input, override-only case, saved
+canonical ambiguity, or execution error. The original lesson, exact programs,
+and intended/rival outputs are retained in the protected execution report.
+
+The current two-depth-anchor schedule correctly addresses the previously
+documented fixed-offset shortcut, but does not force a lesson to teach both
+height parities. `workspace/mirror_teaching_probe.py` supplies a proposed
+`demo_only_survivors` helper for four finite rivals: compressed empty source
+rows, always no center gap, always one center gap with clipping, and only the
+topmost source cell in each column. It inspects demonstration inputs/outputs
+only and propagates execution errors rather than treating them as refutations.
+
+A verified repair proposal appends a distinct already sampled demonstration:
+seed 0/index 0, height 6, width 10. Its protected reference output refutes the
+one-gap rival, and the resulting four demonstrations eliminate all four tested
+rivals. The candidate was selected by demonstration disagreement only and is
+distinct from every input in the original lesson. Production lesson assembly
+has not adopted this guard or parity coverage, so the finding remains open.
+
+The complete bounded scope was two ordinary seeds, 0 and 1, indices 0–7 each:
+16 generated inputs. For each seed, indices 0–2 were demonstrations and 3–6
+were four queries; index 7 was an additional candidate. The saved canonical
+three-demo lesson was replayed separately. A row-compaction rival survives the
+saved canonical and seed-0 demonstrations, but agrees on all of their queried
+inputs; those are not reported as query ambiguities. No unsupported universal
+uniqueness claim is made.
+
+Exact command, from the outer packet directory:
+
+```sh
